@node Document Overview
@chapter Document Overview

The course Applied Cloud Computing and Big Data is a 7.5 ECTS course offered by Blekinge Institute of Technology. The course is organised around three themes@comma{} and all three themes must be completed to complete the course:

@itemize
@item
Cloud Provisioning and Deployment
@item
The Business Case for Cloud Computing
@item
Big Data Analytics
@end itemize

The course is divided across two source code repositories:

@itemize
@item
@uref{https://github.com/mickesv/ProvisioningDeployment.git} contains the instructions and source code for the Cloud Provisioning and Deployment@comma{} and the Business Case for Cloud Computing parts of the course.
@item
@uref{https://github.com/mickesv/BigDataAnalytics.git} contains the instructions and source code for the Big Data Analytics part of the course.
@end itemize

This document covers the first two of these themes@comma{} i.e. Cloud Provisioning and Deployment@comma{} and The Business Case for Cloud Computing. The document is structured as a series of introductions to different topics mixed with hands-on tasks to exercise these topics. 

The topic introductions and practical exercises are further punctuated by quizzes that (a) serve as checkpoints of important concepts that have been covered to that point@comma{} but also (b) introduce further reading material to deepen your understanding of the cloud computing business case. @strong{These quizzes are not marked}@comma{} but serve as a learning aid; for you to summarise what you have learnt so far@comma{} and for us to keep track of your progress through the material.

The two themes are examined through a final assignment (See @ref{assignment-build-something} )@comma{} where you put what you have learnt so far into practice.

This document is available in different formats:

@itemize
@item
as web pages on the course platform
@item
as a pdf file
@item
as a @TeX{}Info tutorial
@end itemize

The @TeX{}Info tutorial may require a bit more introduction. Access this version e.g. through the command @code{info Provisioning-Deployment} or in your favourite editor though @code{C-u C-h i Provisioning-Deployment.info} . Basic navigation in the document is done with the following keys (try @code{info info} for more details and further key commands):

